& [Purpose] is finite inspectable conformance and exact replay without authority collapse
  + materialize every reviewed case expectation claim coverage edge residual edge and reader observation
  + expose mismatches gaps exhaustion faults and nondeterminism
  + make a passing claim only about one exact finite corpus under one exact bound implementation state

& [AuthorityState] is formation_only
  + zero I03E requirements are implemented or verified
  + no corpus case fixture report comparator generator or Rust source is added
  + no satisfaction signature or active phase lock exists

& [PrerequisiteStack] is non-substitutive
  + active completed CPMS-I03A Revision 1 with exact dependency lock and no-resolution proof
  + active completed CPMS-I03B faithful byte ingress
  + active completed CPMS-I03C semantic residual registry
  + active completed CPMS-I03D dual-reader observations
  + exact post-I03D code snapshot Cargo lock I02 bundle I03C registry validator profile and reader profile digests
  + an I03E test cannot compensate for an absent earlier proof

& [RootBinding] retains five distinct roots
  + prepare_input binds exact bytes schema and PrepareRequest deserialization
  + run_input binds exact bytes schema and PreparedRunRequest deserialization
  + verify_input binds exact bytes schema and VerifyRequest deserialization
  + base_response binds an actual ProcedureToolResponse base-intended-use fixture emitted bytes and base schema
  + preparation_response binds an actual ProcedureToolResponse preparation-intended-use fixture emitted bytes and preparation schema
  + shared response Rust type does not merge root claims cases or coverage

& [CorpusAdmission] is atomic
  + verify the exact content-addressed catalogue and fixture inventory before case execution
  + every file path byte length digest role predecessor and provenance is bound by a later activation lock
  + cases claims obligations mappings and fixtures are accepted as one immutable CorpusIdentity
  + a missing duplicate stale dangling or over-limit record refuses the corpus

& [ConformanceCase] is immutable
  + bind case id predecessor root direction family fixture exact expectations applicability claim ids rule ids residual ids obligation ids rationale and provenance
  + input cases own exact bytes
  + response cases own exact typed-fixture identity and expected emitted-byte identity
  + any meaning-bearing mutation creates a successor case rather than overwriting history

& [ExpectationAuthority] is reviewed
  + an LLM generator mutator or tool may propose a case
  + generator identity version seed operator parameters and output digest remain provenance
  + expected dispositions claim mappings and rationale require human review before later signature
  + random fuzz output requires reduction stable identity and review

& [CommonSyntaxClaim] licenses comparison
  + name one JSON-level proposition intentionally represented by both selected readers
  + bind root subject proposition expected disposition applicability and source rationale
  + own a SchemaWitness and TypedWitness because the two readers use different rule vocabularies
  + representation-only semantic intended-use authority and observational propositions are not common syntax claims

& [SchemaWitness] maps claim to normalized schema rule classes locations and finding projections
& [TypedWitness] maps claim to Rust type intended use binding operation destination path and error projection
  + binding operation is deserialize_exact_bytes for input roots
  + binding operation is serialize_actual_value for response roots
  + literal equality of schema and typed rule identifiers is neither required nor sufficient

& [ComparisonTruthTable] is closed
  + accepted_agreement requires both applicable readers ran both were expected accepted both accepted and map to the same claim
  + rejected_agreement requires both applicable readers ran both were expected rejected both rejected and both rejection witnesses map to the same claim
  + reader_disagreement is accepted-rejected or rejected-accepted
  + reason_mismatch is two rejections whose mapped claims differ or cannot be established
  + expectation_mismatch occurs whenever either actual disposition differs from its own expectation even if both actual dispositions match
  + not_comparable occurs when no CommonSyntaxClaim applies and never counts as agreement
  + blocked occurs for prerequisite ingress dependency exhaustion panic or internal fault and never counts as agreement

& [IngressGovernance] precedes comparison
  + invalid UTF-8 malformed JSON trailing data duplicate keys and ingress resource refusal stop later readers for that case
  + their expected refusal can satisfy an ingress obligation
  + skipped schema and typed observations remain skipped_dependency rather than not_applicable
  + duplicate-key collapse behavior is never represented as schema-typed agreement

& [SemanticEvaluation] is orthogonal
  + execute only an I03C safe_pure binding with exact module function code snapshot input type proof and resource profile
  + execute only after a complete admitted fixture exists
  + observational_only yields a non-executing observation
  + prohibited_authority and unimplemented yield refusal without invocation
  + semantic result is compared to semantic expectation but never participates in syntax agreement

& [CorpusFamilies] are fully accounted
  + C00 canonical positive minimum representative and actual response serialization
  + C01 byte framing malformed duplicate and ingress limits
  + C02 required optional null unknown type enum and tag object contracts
  + C03 exact numeric token schema range and Rust destination boundaries
  + C04 collection recursive ingress typed and local-reference boundaries
  + C05 semantic id digest authorship identity and lineage substitutions
  + C06 generation transition replay token-holder participant transcript and receipt mutations
  + C07 no-capability external-reference refusal and response-shape contradictions
  + every family-root-rule relation is satisfied not_applicable or a visible deferred coverage gap

& [CoverageObligation] is exact
  + bind root rule family polarity below-at-above position applicability mandatory severity and source
  + each satisfied relation is an explicit CoverageEdge to a case and claim
  + reconstruct coverage from edges rather than trusting summary counters
  + percentage is advisory and zero uncovered mandatory obligations is authoritative for pass

& [ResidualCoverage] is exact
  + resolve all twenty I03C residual identities through the bound registry
  + map each applicable residual to case evidence a reviewed not-applicable relation or visible deferred gap
  + preserve enforcement disposition and evaluation policy byte-for-byte
  + never infer residual enforcement from schema or typed agreement

& [CaseExecution] is deterministic
  + lexical case-id order
  + immutable bound inputs and no ambient configuration
  + I03B ingress then I03D readers according to applicability then optional safe pure semantic binding
  + comparison expectation and coverage reconstruction after observations are complete
  + expected case rejection records evidence and does not abort later cases

& [ObservationPreservation] is lossless
  + carry ReaderPair identity and complete original schema and typed observations
  + never rewrite finding paths numeric projection representation fault or residual disposition
  + comparison records point to observations rather than replacing them

& [FindingProjection] is stable
  + kinds expectation_mismatch reader_disagreement reason_mismatch residual_gap coverage_gap exhaustion nondeterminism and internal_fault
  + finding id binds profile case kind reader claim rule path residual set expected and actual stable dispositions
  + bounded diagnostic is advisory and library-generated text is excluded from identity
  + normative order is case kind reader claim rule schema path residual ids finding id

& [ReportCore] is one pure-run projection
  + binds profile corpus bundle registry validator reader code and lock digests
  + owns ordered case evaluations comparisons semantic records findings coverage residual and resource accounts
  + disposition is passed refused exhausted or internal_fault
  + contains no self digest timestamp wall-clock duration host path address thread order random seed ambient environment or engine display field

& [CanonicalReportEncoding] is fixed
  + UTF-8 JSON without BOM whitespace or trailing newline
  + fixed object-member order and complete lexical collection sort keys
  + base-10 integers without leading zeros and no floating-point report field
  + one specified JSON string-escaping profile and uppercase hexadecimal digests
  + core digest is domain-separated SHA256 over exact core bytes

& [ExactReplay] runs the whole pure DAG twice
  + do not clone or reuse first-run result objects as second-run evidence
  + bind identical profile catalogue fixture code lock and prerequisite identities
  + canonicalize ReportCore A and freshly recomputed ReportCore B independently
  + require byte equality and digest equality
  + inequality creates nondeterminism and final internal_fault

& [ReplayEnvelope] is non-circular
  + payload binds schema exact input identity first core digest second core digest byte equality and disposition
  + envelope digest is domain-separated SHA256 over canonical payload bytes
  + envelope never contains a digest over bytes that already contain that same digest field

& [PassRule] is conjunctive
  + every expected reader and semantic observation matches
  + every licensed comparison has its expected disposition
  + zero findings
  + zero uncovered mandatory obligations
  + zero dangling applicable residuals
  + all resource accounts are exact and within limits
  + both ReportCore byte sequences are identical
  + pass means only finite corpus conformance for the bound identities

& [Limits] are inherited and explicit
  + cases 4096 aggregate fixture bytes 67108864 findings per case 256 diagnostic characters per finding 1024
  + input schema typed residual path reference recursion and report limits remain separately authoritative
  + all counts offsets lengths products forecasts and allocations use checked arithmetic
  + exhaustion prevents pass and preserves unexecuted case identities

& [FailureAtomicity] is strict
  + stale identity malformed catalogue duplicate id dangling edge unsupported claim skipped dependency overflow resource exhaustion or internal fault blocks pass
  + prerequisite failure permits only one bounded fault envelope and no partial coverage claim
  + failed evaluation never publishes a passing or partial canonical corpus report

& [FutureSourceTouch] is unsigned and must become file-exact at activation
  + modify crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/lib.rs under active schema-conformance
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance_report.rs
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/conformance_report.rs
  + add one content-addressed compile-time corpus catalogue and fixture tree
  + activation lock lists every added path length digest role and lineage
  + test writes no report fixture cache database or runtime file

& [Proof] after future activation is layered
  + exact source and catalogue inventory replay
  + five-root C00 through C07 obligation accounting
  + accepted rejected disagreement reason-mismatch expectation-mismatch not-comparable and blocked truth-table witnesses
  + input deserialization and distinct response-intended-use serialization witnesses
  + all twenty residual coverage reconstruction
  + below-at-above resource and numeric boundaries
  + first and second complete pure execution with exact canonical byte equality
  + locked offline debug release format lint docs audit evidence and exact diff review

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + this slice adds only preserved source SJS canonical exploded requirements justification plan review inactive lock proof narrative and evidence metadata
  - never: Cargo dependency Rust corpus fixture generator reader comparator semantic execution compatibility certification admission provider model service persistence runtime file network notification external effect production release hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [Disposition] is canonical_formation_complete_implementation_refused
